# Mandalon
SvelteKit remake of [mandalon.se](https://mandalon.se). B2B site for chip packaging, bonding, and consulting services.
## Stack
- **Svelte 5** with runes mode forced project-wide (`$props()`, `$derived()`, `{@render children()}`)
- **SvelteKit 2** with **Vite 5**
- **Node 18.20.8** (see `.nvmrc`)
- **Adapter:** `@sveltejs/adapter-node`
- **TypeScript** throughout (`lang="ts"` in Svelte; `.ts` for lib modules and route loaders)
- **Lint/format:** ESLint + Prettier (`npm run lint`, `npm run format`)
- **Type check:** `npm run check` (svelte-check via `tsconfig.json`)
- **Line endings:** LF only (Unix newlines) — enforced via `.gitattributes` (`* text=auto eol=lf`). Do not use CRLF (carriage return). New and edited files must end lines with `\n` only.
## Commands
```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # local development
npm run build    # production build
npm run check    # svelte-check
npm run check:build # smoke-check prerendered build output
npm run lint     # prettier + eslint
npm run format   # Perform formatting, prettier + svelte
```
## i18n and routing

- Public pages live under `src/routes/(site)/(sv)/` (Swedish, no URL prefix) and `src/routes/(site)/en/` (English under `/en/…`)
- Swedish is default (`/paketering`); English uses translated slugs (`/en/packaging`)
- Route groups: `(site)` for public pages, `(sv)` / `en` for locales, `(stats)` for `/stats`, `(dev)` for `/experiment` and `/fonts` (dev only) — parentheses do not appear in URLs
- **Slugs:** `src/lib/routes.ts` is the only place URL slugs may be defined. Build hrefs with `hrefFor(pageKey, locale)`. Do not hardcode path strings for in-site links.
- Content: per-page modules in `src/lib/content/pages/*.ts` (both locales adjacent in each file); `src/lib/content/site.ts` assembles `siteContent`. Locale layouts pass `data.content` to pages
- Content shapes live in `src/lib/content/types.ts`
- Canonical pages use Swedish slugs under `(sv)/`; EN routes under `en/` are thin wrappers that import the SV page (see `svelte-components.mdc`)
- Site chrome (`SiteChrome`, header, footer, hreflang) wraps `(site)` pages; document metadata via `PageMeta`

## Conventions

- **Content:** User-facing text lives in `src/lib/content/` — pages consume it as `data.content`; components receive content via props (never hardcoded). Shared English-only bodies (e.g. design guide article) may live in a dedicated module under `pages/`
- **Code comments:** Swedish or English
- **Reference page:** `(site)/(sv)/paketering/+page.svelte` — canonical example of page structure
- **Before done:** After any code change, run `npm run format`, then `npm run check`, then `npm run lint`. Do not consider the task done until all three pass. If the change touches routing, loaders, layouts, hooks, prerendering, or the document head, also run `npm run build` and `npm run check:build`.
